"comparison": "Both JPM and BAC disclose the fair value of unencumbered securities as a key liquidity source and note that borrowing against these assets provides incremental liquidity. However, JPM reports a total stock of $594 billion in unencumbered marketable securities at year-end 2024, which decreased from the prior year. In contrast, BAC reports a specific borrowing capacity of $328 billion derived from pledging unencumbered loans and securities at its bank subsidiaries at year-end 2024, an increase from $312 billion in 2023. BAC also highlights regulatory restrictions that generally limit the use of this liquidity to bank subsidiary obligations, whereas JPM notes that while some excess HQLA is non-transferable, the broader unencumbered securities are believed to be available to raise liquidity.",
